so the program neither links against CloudXR nor needs it to build. The
\emph{device profile} tells the service what kind of client to expect, and
with it the eye resolution and frame rate: [[apple-vision-pro]] and
[[quest3]] are static profiles, whose OpenXR system exists as soon as the
service starts, while the [[auto-*]] profiles wait for a client to connect
and then adopt its parameters.

